{"availability":"available","full":"hermes98761234/print-cost-estimator","name":"print-cost-estimator","description":"3D print cost and time estimator: load an STL, get material weight, print time and a price quote. Runs in your browser.","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-10T05:30:09Z","updated":"2026-10-10T05:30:21Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://hermes98761234.github.io/print-cost-estimator/","topics":["3d-printing","cost-calculator","gcode","github-pages","react","stl","typescript","vite"],"demo":"https://hermes98761234.github.io/print-cost-estimator/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T07:04:13.637Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T07:04:13.637Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T07:04:13.637Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T07:04:13.637Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["React"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["What will this 3D print cost? Load an STL (or OBJ), pick a filament or resin, and get the model's volume and surface area, the material weight and filament length, an estimated print time and a full price quote: material, electricity, machine depreciation, labor, failure allowance, markup and tax. Optionally load the sliced G-code to use the slicer's own time and filament numbers. Everything runs in your browser.","Try it: hermes98761234.github.io/print-cost-estimator"],"features":["STL (binary and ASCII) and OBJ, with a drag-to-rotate preview, bounding box, volume, surface area and triangle count. Warns about open (non-watertight) meshes and inverted normals. Built-in samples load instantly.","Material presets: PLA, PETG, ABS, ASA, TPU, Nylon and standard resin, each with an editable density and price per kg.","Material from walls and infill: wall count and line width, top/bottom layers, infill percentage, supports and waste/purge percentages. Resin supports solid or hollowed models.","Time estimate from a volumetric flow limit, layer overhead and warm-up, or from G-code: the slicer's own estimate (Cura, PrusaSlicer/SuperSlicer, OrcaSlicer/Bambu Studio, Simplify3D comments) and filament use, or a…","Quote: material, electricity (average power), machine depreciation (price over lifetime), labor, failure allowance, markup, tax, quantity and per-unit price. Copy it as text, download a .txt, or print / save as PDF."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/hermes98761234/print-cost-estimator/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"ff2b2efbbd7de2f98530fdfcd9e01a9e37573bfa22d7919b0d09cef8fb7b11ff","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T07:04:13.704Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T07:04:13.704Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"What will this 3D print cost? Load an STL (or OBJ), pick a filament or resin, and get the model's volume and surface area, the material weight and filament length, an estimated print time and a full price quote: material, electricity, machine depreciation, labor, failure allowance, markup and tax. Optionally load the sliced G-code to use the slicer's own time and filament numbers. Everything runs in your browser.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/hermes98761234/print-cost-estimator/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"ff2b2efbbd7de2f98530fdfcd9e01a9e37573bfa22d7919b0d09cef8fb7b11ff","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/hermes98761234/print-cost-estimator/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T07:04:13.705Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-10T05:30:21Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/hermes98761234/print-cost-estimator/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T07:04:13.705Z","hash":"ff2b2efbbd7de2f98530fdfcd9e01a9e37573bfa22d7919b0d09cef8fb7b11ff","originalBytes":3357,"storedBytes":3357,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["material","volume","print","time","area","cost","filament","g-code","infill","layer","load","npm","browser.","depreciation","each","electricity","estimate","failure","labor","line